# ~/.claude is ~2,600 files of machine state (transcripts, caches, locks, cloned plugin
# repos) wrapped around ~180 files of hand-written config — plus a live OAuth token in
# .credentials.json. So: ignore everything, then opt back in by name.
#
# Adding a new hand-authored file or directory? It needs a `!` line here or git will
# never see it. To find anything currently invisible:
#   git status --porcelain --ignored | grep '^!!'

*

# --- Config ---
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!PLAN.md
!settings.json
!justfile

# --- Planning system state: the north star and the per-feature spec docs ---
!docs/
!docs/**

# --- Hand-authored directories ---
# Both lines per directory are required: `!dir/` lets git descend into it, `!dir/**`
# re-includes the contents (bare `*` above matches at every depth, not just the root).
!agents/
!agents/**
!commands/
!commands/**
!guidelines/
!guidelines/**
!hooks/
!hooks/**
!skills/
!skills/**
!templates/
!templates/**

# hooks/ interleaves per-session state with the scripts. Must come after !hooks/**.
hooks/state/

# Installed and overwritten by herdr's integration; not ours to version.
hooks/herdr-agent-state.sh

# Skill-sync store and its trash. Rewrites a manifest timestamp every sync round.
skills/.trash/
skills/synced/

# --- Plugin manifests: enough to restore the plugin set on a new machine.
# The cloned marketplace repos under plugins/marketplaces/ stay ignored — they carry
# their own .git directories and would be committed as broken gitlinks.
# known_marketplaces.json stays ignored too: it rewrites a lastUpdated timestamp on
# every marketplace refresh, so it is churn, not config.
!plugins/
!plugins/installed_plugins.json

# --- projects/*/memory/ is deliberately NOT opted back in ---
# This repo is public, and the memory notes name client work, internal servers and
# unpublished research. They stay on this machine only; Claude Code reads them from disk.

# --- Never, at any depth, even inside an allowed directory ---
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.bak-*
.credentials.json
